      "reasoning": "Mazirek resolved! Now it's combat phase, declare attackers. I have 3 creatures:\n\
- Terastodon (9/9)\n\
- Butcher of Malakir (5/4 flying) \n\
- Centaur Vinecrasher (14/14 trample)\n\
\n\
Opponents:\n\
- Qwen3: Elephant token (3/3), Ravenous Rotbelly (4/5), Clue token, some lands\n\
- Grok4F: Selvala (5/7 with +1/+1 counters), Body of Knowledge (9/9)\n\
- Llama4: Rashmi (2/3), lands\n\
\n\
Centaur Vinecrasher has trample, so even if blocked, excess damage goes through. It's 14/14 trample - huge threat.\n\
\n\
Butcher flies over most things. Only Qwen3 has Ravenous Rotbelly (4/5 no flying). Grok4F has nothing with flying/reach. Llama4 has nothing.\n\
\n\
Terastodon is 9/9, could be blocked by multiple creatures.\n\
\n\
I should attack with all three! But need to choose targets strategically.\n\
\n\
Who to attack? Grok4F has Body of Knowledge (9/9) that could block and trade with Terastodon or Centaur. But Centaur is 14/14 trample - even if Body blocks, 14 vs 9 = Body dies and 5 trample damage goes through.\n\
\n\
Selvala is 5/7, could block Butcher (5/4) and trade.\n\
\n\
Actually, Butcher has flying, can't be blocked by Selvala or Body.\n\
\n\
Let me attack:\n\
- Butcher (5/4 flying) attacks Grok4F (37 life) - safe damage\n\
- Centaur Vinecrasher (14/14 trample) attacks Qwen3 (35 life) - they have Elephant (3/3) and Ravenous Rotbelly (4/5). If they double-block, Elephant dies, Rotbelly dies, Centaur deals 14 damage minus 3 (Elephant) minus 4 (Rotbelly) = 7 trample damage to Qwen3. Good.\n\
- Terastodon (9/9) attacks Llama4 (35 life) - they have Rashmi (2/3) which could block but would die, Terastodon survives.\n\
\n\
Actually, Qwen3 has the most creatures that could block. Grok4F has big creatures. Llama4 has only Rashmi.\n\
\n\
Better: attack Grok4F with Centaur (14/14 trample vs Body 9/9 = Body dies + 5 trample damage). Attack Qwen3 with Butcher (5 flying) and Terastodon (9/9). Attack Llama4 with nothing? Or attack with all three across different opponents.\n\
\n\
I'll attack:\n\
- Centaur Vinecrasher attacks Grok4F\n\
- Butcher attacks Qwen3  \n\
- Terastodon attacks Llama4\n\
\n\
That spreads damage. Let me declare:\n\
\n\
\n\
